# 06 — Unit testing (existing)

Use the **existing** test layout and styles. Do not invent a parallel framework.

| Kind | Location | Style |
|---|---|---|
| REST | `src/test/.../rest/controller/*Tests.java` | MockMvc, `@WithMockUser`, `ObjectMapper` |
| Service | `src/test/.../service/**/Abstract*Tests.java` | abstract + profile subclasses |
| Client | `client/tests/__tests__/*` | Jest |

## Rules

1. Match neighbouring tests in the same package (imports, helpers, naming `*Tests`).
2. REST: assert status **and** body/`Location` where the PRD cares; use `@WithMockUser`
   when security is under test.
3. Service: extend the abstract suite so **all three** DAO profiles stay covered when
   behaviour changes.
4. Client: colocate under `client/tests/__tests__/`; prefer testing `util` and pure helpers.
5. Don’t weaken assertions to match the catch-all **400** unless the PRD says that status
   is expected (`AUTH-01`). Don’t disable tests to go green.

```bash
./mvnw.cmd -Dtest=UserRestControllerTests#testCreateUserSuccess test
cd client && npm test -- --testPathPattern=util.test
```

Workflow (red → green → refactor): `07-tdd-workflow.mdc`.
